{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>Why did you not eat the sin-offering in the holy place.</b> Did they eat it outside the holy place? Was it not burned? And what does he mean by 'in the holy place'? Rather, he said to them: perhaps it went outside the hangings and was disqualified." "<b>For it is most holy.</b> And it is disqualified by going out, and they said to him: no. He said to them: since it was in the holy place, why did you not eat it?" "<b>And He gave it to you to bear, etc.</b> That the priests eat and the owners obtain atonement." "<b>To bear the iniquity of the congregation.</b> From this we learn that it was the goat of the new moon, for it atones for the iniquity of impurity of the Temple and its holy things — for the sin-offering of the eighth day and the sin-offering of Nachshon did not come for atonement."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:05:42.323670225Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}